  "summary": "Name places in town, say where you are going and what you are going to do, and give simple directions. Learn each place with its article: la gare, le parc, l'école.",
  "canDo": [
    "Name places in town with the right article: la gare, le parc, l'école.",
    "Say where I am going, using aller with au, à la, à l' or aux.",
    "Talk about what I am going to do soon, using aller and a verb: je vais manger.",
    "Ask where a place is and give simple directions: à gauche, à droite, tout droit."
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u09-l1",
      "title": "Places",
      "goal": "Name places in town and say what they are like.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "u09-l1-n1",
          "title": "Every place has an article",
          "body": "Each place is a noun, so it is **masculine** or **feminine**. Use **le** for a masculine place, **la** for a feminine one, and **l'** before a vowel sound. Learn each place with its article: *le parc*, *la gare*, *l'école*. The adjective agrees with the place: *grand* for a masculine place, *grande* for a feminine one.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Le parc est beau, non ?",
              "en": "The park is nice, isn't it?"
            },
            {
              "fr": "La maison est petite.",
              "en": "The house is small."
            },
            {
              "fr": "L'école est grande.",
              "en": "The school is big."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u09-l1-n2",
          "title": "Places in the plural",
          "body": "For more than one place, use **les** and add **-s** to the noun. The **-s** is silent. The adjective also takes **-s** for a masculine plural, and **-es** for a feminine plural: *grand* becomes *grands*, and *grande* becomes *grandes*.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Les écoles sont grandes.",
              "en": "The schools are big."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Les parcs sont beaux.",
              "en": "The parks are nice."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Les villes sont belles, non ?",
              "en": "The cities are beautiful, aren't they?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
