    {
      "id": "u09-l2",
      "title": "To go",
      "goal": "Say where you are going, using aller and à with the article.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "u09-l2-n1",
          "title": "Aller: to go",
          "body": "**Aller** means *to go*. It is irregular, so learn the forms: **je vais**, tu vas, il/elle va, nous allons, vous allez, ils/elles vont. Use it with **à** and a place to say where you are going.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Je vais au parc.",
              "en": "I am going to the park."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Tu vas à la gare ?",
              "en": "Are you going to the station?"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Nous allons à la maison.",
              "en": "We are going home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u09-l2-n2",
          "title": "À + the article",
          "body": "**à** means *to* or *at*. Before **le** it joins into **au**, and before **les** it joins into **aux**. Before **la** and before a vowel it stays as **à la** and **à l'**. Learn each place with its phrase: *au parc*, *à la gare*, *à l'école*, *aux parcs*.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Je vais au supermarché.",
              "en": "I am going to the supermarket."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Ils vont aux parcs.",
              "en": "They are going to the parks."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Tu vas à l'école ?",
              "en": "Are you going to school?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "words": [
        {
