      "title": "Directions",
      "goal": "Ask where a place is and give simple directions.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "u09-l4-n1",
          "title": "Où est… ? Where is…?",
          "body": "To ask where a place is, say **où est** and the place: *Où est la gare ?* For more than one place, say **où sont**: *Où sont les écoles ?* The answer uses **est** or **sont** in the same way: *La gare est…*",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Où est la gare, madame ?",
              "en": "Where is the station, madam?"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Où est le parc ?",
              "en": "Where is the park?"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Où sont les écoles ?",
              "en": "Where are the schools?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u09-l4-n2",
          "title": "Left, right and straight on",
          "body": "**À gauche** means *on the left*, **à droite** means *on the right*, and **tout droit** means *straight ahead*. **Près** means *near* and **loin** means *far*. Put them after **est**: *Le parc est à droite.*",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Tout droit, monsieur.",
              "en": "Straight ahead, sir."
            },
            {
              "fr": "La gare est à gauche.",
              "en": "The station is on the left."
            },
            {
              "fr": "L'école est loin.",
              "en": "The school is far."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
